Metadata/transport, FEL, Master Reference and shared processing API files
marked GPL-3.0-or-later retain that license.

Original HDR10 AI, model-adapter, circuit and policy modules are now offered
under GPL-2.0-or-later by their owner. Replacement cache, metadata-bounds,
serializer and CM4 wire helpers use GPL-2.0-or-later. Retained third-party notices still apply.
The replacement canonical tunnel shader, GL packer, vertex and generated-source
wrapper use GPL-2.0-or-later. Fused renderer packing remains under its prior terms.

Original frame transactions, Master Reference contract, processing preparation,
GL frame adapter and CPU Adaptive model use GPL-2.0-or-later under the owner's
grant. This does not relicense their separately implemented dependencies.

The scalar creative module combines original CM4/resolver/fitter code with
replacement numerical kernels under GPL-2.0-or-later; see the migration record.

The original Adaptive compute shader and replacement GPU trim/carrier kernels
use GPL-2.0-or-later. The retained fused colour/composition adapter in
dvbridge_render.c is GPL-3.0-only. The shared static-library combination is
therefore conveyed under GPL-3.0-only, retaining each file's original notices.

Original tooling/documentation is MIT where declared. The FFmpeg-derived filter
retains LGPL-2.1-or-later. Dependency patches include both inherited LGPL code and
explicit GPL-3.0-or-later additions; see docs/LICENSE-MAP.md.

The exact L1/L3 model bundle is offered under GPL-2.0-or-later by its owner.
LightGBM itself is MIT. See models/l1l3/LICENSE.md.

